; resize_beyond_size: a grid may not describe cells the register never
; declared.
;
; A grid is a reinterpretation of variables the program already allocated
; and already paid for, so `rows * cols` may not exceed the model or
; sample's size. Without the bound this twenty-two byte program is
; verifier-clean and runs for geological time: the ROWSUM that follows
; scans 2^62 cells for one metered step and charges nothing, so a caller
; who pre-pays ten steps buys an execution that never finishes.
;
; The rule is `<=` rather than `==`, because EQUALITY, ATLEAST, ATLEASTW
; and REDUCE append slack and auxiliary variables past the grid.

PUSH 4
BQMX r0

PUSH 1                        ; rows
PUSH 4611686018427387904      ; cols = 2^62
RESIZE r0

PUSH 0                        ; row
ROWSUM r0
HALT
